{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0000", "block": 0, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 50, "sha256": "411cb5679aa58dc4", "text": "Copilot Remote Code Execution via Prompt Injection"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0001", "block": 1, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 242, "sha256": "2b66cfcf09acfc28", "text": "This post is about an important, but also scary, prompt injection discovery that leads to full system compromise of the developer’s machine in [GitHub Copilot and VS Code](https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2025-53773)."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0002", "block": 2, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 101, "sha256": "5a35b01f5cd68a98", "text": "**It is achieved by placing Copilot into YOLO mode by modifying the project’s `settings.json` file.**"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0003", "block": 3, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 94, "sha256": "4bbd52fd475c40b2", "text": "[![vscode episode 18](/blog/images/2025/episode12-yt.png)](/blog/images/2025/episode12-yt.png)"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0004", "block": 4, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 409, "sha256": "fd625cc7acaca950", "text": "As described a few days ago with [Amp](/blog/posts/2025/amp-agents-that-modify-system-configuration-and-escape/), a vulnerability pattern in agents that might be overlooked is that if an agent can write to files and modify its own configuration or update security-relevant settings it can lead to remote code execution. This is not uncommon and is an area to always look for when performing a security review."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0005", "block": 5, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 19, "sha256": "26b267151f7dd974", "text": "Background Research"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0006", "block": 6, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 156, "sha256": "2d909819444f753a", "text": "When looking at VS Code and GitHub Copilot Agent Mode I noticed a strange behavior… it can create and write to files in the workspace without user approval."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0007", "block": 7, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 131, "sha256": "36f54e2919691908", "text": "The edits are immediately persistent, they are not in-memory as a diff to review. The modifications are written to disk right away."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0008", "block": 8, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 131, "sha256": "d7ec7e8b41a6f8a5", "text": "[![vscode agents that can modify their own settings](/blog/images/2025/agents-that-can.png)](/blog/images/2025/agents-that-can.png)"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0009", "block": 9, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 156, "sha256": "ca7e16d763b5c02b", "text": "It’s one of these things that as a red teamer you know is probably not good… so I was looking if this could be used to escalate privileges and execute code."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0010", "block": 10, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 13, "sha256": "235aaa0038acef0d", "text": "**YOLO Mode**"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0011", "block": 11, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 149, "sha256": "e5773374bc1d3cd9", "text": "So, next I researched features in VS Code that depend on settings that are within the project/workspace folder, and quickly found an interesting one."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0012", "block": 12, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 141, "sha256": "dff21beebafd20d8", "text": "[![vscode-exp-yolo-mode](/blog/images/2025/vscode-documentation-settings-json.png)](/blog/images/2025/vscode-documentation-settings-json.png)"}
