{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0014", "block": 14, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 32, "sha256": "e38f52836264c48d", "text": "`\"chat.tools.autoApprove\": true`"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0015", "block": 15, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 46, "sha256": "d18be0755e148cd7", "text": "**This will put GitHub Copilot in YOLO mode.**"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0016", "block": 16, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 96, "sha256": "0d756cf6034616f2", "text": "And it disables all user confirmations, and we can run shell commands, browse the web, and more!"}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0017", "block": 17, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 186, "sha256": "c4d2e922b427a417", "text": "What is interesting is that this is an experimental feature, but it is still present by default. I did not download a special version or set my VS Code overall into an experimental mode."}
{"slug": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio", "id": "embracethered-com-blog-posts-2025-github-copilot-remote-code-execution-via-prompt-injectio#b0018", "block": 18, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 55, "sha256": "ba2df458b470c7d8", "text": "Furthermore, it works on Windows, macOS and also Linux."}
